Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Async output used to drift with worker timing (en->zh 3-21 lines, pivot
16-30 lines per 150-200 differ from blocking). Requests are now built on the
calling thread and enqueued under one lock; pivot's second leg waits for the
whole first leg. A submission too small to give every worker a batch is split
by a deterministic sentence cap so it still runs in parallel; anything larger
is byte-identical to BlockingService at every worker count. requestId_ was a
plain size_t written from worker threads in pivot callbacks.

